{"id":"000W7X","title":"Grave Misinformation (Infections)","author":"gdc","solvedCount":6,"difficulty":4,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-27T22:03:54+00:00","posted":"Heute, 18:24 Uhr","rules":"Episode 7 of the Norma L. Dokes series. Based on the pencil puzzle type Yajisan-Kazusan. According to testers (thanks everyone!) difficulty should be around 4 stars. Enjoy!\n\nRules\n\nNormal sudoku rules apply.\n\nInfection Sources: Each digit matching its box number is an \"infection source\". Each row and column contains an infection source. They are infected.\n\nTransmission: Infected cells infect all smaller orthogonal neighbors. This process repeats until no further infections are possible.\n\nHealthy Network: All uninfected cells must form a single orthogonally connected area.\n\nCircles: A digit in an uninfected circle counts the number of infected cells in all indicated directions combined. (Infected circles may or may not be lying.)\n\nClick on the image to play!\n\nExample Puzzle\n\nA 6x6 puzzle with the same rules. Colors: Orange for infection sources, red for other infected, and green for uninfected.","solutionCode":"Infected cells in column 5, top to bottom (up to 8 digits). For the example puzzle, this would be 213.","tags":["Sudoku","Yajisan-Kazusan","Fortress (Variante)","Modifier Cells (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/thz28rx0ta","kind":"sudokupad"},{"url":"https://tinyurl.com/normaldokes","kind":"short"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/thz28rx0ta","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines","overlays","underlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-27T22:03:54+00:00"}